														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2235316">
									

<p>I like this on the whole, but one thing I'm ambivalent about is the complexity of the criteria for what animals do and don't work. It makes me think, which is usually a plus in my book, but it makes me think about things which I'm not sure are really the 'point' of the SCP, if that makes sense? Kind of distracts from the point, in other words?</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<p>- Do controversial foods like oysters work for some people and not others?<br />
- If an individual person is, for whatever reason, creeped out by ordinary animals such as dogs, would they be able to read dog thoughts by drinking dog hair?<br />
- Can someone be creeped out by the human species? Could it be leveraged into human telepathy?<br />
- Would it work on anomalous nonsentient animals or sentient beings, provided the drinker is sufficiently creeped out by them?</p>
<p>I am by far NOT an expert on writing good SCPs so I don't think that necessarily test logs need to be added to answer these questions, I'm just kinda expressing where my mind went, here</p>

							</div>

								
					
